# .gitignore — TaskDira Backend
# Scoped to Backend/ deliberately: the repo root is shared with Frontend/,
# which is owned by another team (CLAUDE.md 10).

## Build output
bin/
obj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]/
[Aa][Rr][Mm]64/

## NuGet
*.nupkg
*.snupkg
project.lock.json

## Test and coverage artifacts
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
*.trx
*.coverage
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
coverage*.info

## IDE / editor
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

## Secrets — never commit (CLAUDE.md 4.6)
# Real values live in .NET user-secrets locally (stored outside the repo, under
# %APPDATA%\Microsoft\UserSecrets) and in environment variables when deployed.
# appsettings.json and appsettings.Development.json stay tracked on purpose:
# they hold non-sensitive defaults only. These patterns catch the file names
# people reach for when they need somewhere to put a real connection string.
.env
.env.*
appsettings.Local.json
appsettings.*.Local.json
appsettings.Secrets.json
secrets.json
*.pfx
*.p12
*.pem
*.key

## OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# The pinned local tool manifest MUST stay tracked — it is how the team gets
# the same dotnet-ef 9.x (CLAUDE.md 2). Guard against a future `.config/` rule.
!.config/dotnet-tools.json
